  "query_preview": "../Thursday through Sunday/...\nWednesday will see the tail end of an active weather pattern from\na low pressure system in the gulf, with rain and wind diminishing\nthrough the day. This low is expected to move south out of the \narea through the day Thursday, which looks to be a period of drier\nconditions and calmer winds. The upper level flow looks to shift \nto be more southerly, but not fully offshore, so the southern \npanhandle, especially, could see more showery conditions. Late \nFriday or overnight into Saturday, another front looks to move \nacross the panhandle, bringing elevated winds back to the inner \nchannels, up to about 20-25kts, with periods of heavier rain. This\nsystem is not expected to bring unseasonable amounts of rain, so \nthere is no major flooding concern at this time.",
